@snaik20 

> Are currently working on this PR. I'm interested in this feature and would be happy to continue the work.

Hi, I haven't had a chance to work on this PR the last couple of months. I remember there were a couple of comments in the review. If you want to help address them that would be great.

Given that we want to merge this into the next release, *before* any of the code rewrites to Compose/Kotlin, we have to make sure we can merge it into the rewrite branch cleanly.

@snaik20 you converted some existing player files (e.g. PlayerService) to kotlin in https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipe/pull/9592/commits/9da43afd5ff3faeb77b53f704372742992303372
I think we should revert this in this PR for now so that we can cleanly merge into the rewrite branch later (without too many lines changed)

Code looks good to me now, except these two review comments that still need to be resolved: https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipe/pull/9592#discussion_r1930646888, https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipe/pull/9592#discussion_r1864794286. The diff below includes a fix for the first review comment plus some more refactorings related to null stuff (plus some unrelated things you may use for testing), so you can use that if you want.

However, while testing out the app, I noticed a few bugs related to `PlayerService`.
1. The player service (and the player itself) are started in the background as soon as the app is opened when connected to a car
2. The player service, even after `stopSelf()` and `onDestroy()` have been called, still remains alive somewhere in the Android OS (I checked all places where we keep it in our app and we handle it correctly everywhere; I also confirmed this with LeakCanary).
3. Whenever the player service has already been destroyed once, if you then open another video (which would start the player service again), either nothing happens or the app crashes because the LocalBinder corresponding to the old service also remained alive in the background for some reason. Full steps to reproduce: open a video from the car, close the video from the car with the X, open a video from the phone.
4. Closing a video with the X in the bottom right corner from the phone (with VideoDetailFragment collapsed in the bottom sheet) while the car is connected only closes the VideoDetailFragment without stopping the player (i.e. playback continues).

Would it be possible to move the `MediaBrowserServiceCompat` interface to a separate service? For such a service it would be totally fine if it keeps running in the background and never be stopped. But the player service was never meant to be like that, hence the crashes and strange behavior. I'm not sure if problem 4. is related to this though, it needs to be investigated separately I believe.

Fortunately none of these problems seem to exist while using the app when a car is not connected (at least on my phone and on the emulator).

